 "reading": "Unfreezing the VLM and vision encoder (plastic) on the same v5a data lifts the frozen-suite success at every checkpoint: 2.5k 0.29 (baseline 0.11, +0.18 [+0.07, +0.29], p = 0.002), 5k 0.24 (0.09, +0.15, p = 0.0015), 7.5k 0.31 [0.23, 0.41] (0.16, +0.15 [+0.05, +0.26], p = 0.011; against the baseline's 10k 0.10: +0.21, p = 0.0001), selected 7.5k (all within CI). The variations move with it (camera_shift 0.34, far 0.18, lighting 0.24, target_relocation 0.30: +0.11 to +0.19 over the baseline's 10k, all p < 0.05), blank image 0.01, and within plastic the pattern matches the other single-camera runs (camera_shift not separable from nominal, far -0.13, gain 0.61 -0.05 inside the noise). Confounds: 75k samples seen (batch 8 x 9.4k) against the baseline's 320k, and 9.4k of 10k steps; both cut against plastic, so the gain is not an artefact of more training. Reading: representation updates buy about 15 points on a single third-person view (the Z-1 argument that perception-limited failures need VLM updates), but the wrist camera buys 79 points on a frozen VLM (v6 10k 0.89 vs plastic 7.5k 0.31: +0.58 [+0.47, +0.68], 61 vs 3 discordant) - the sensing lever dominates the representation lever by a factor of four at this budget, and a plastic run on v6 is the natural next variant."
